2|0@atheism^1438613713#ctpxhxg:enjoycarrots$:Religion is not a rigidly defined word. It's definition is arbitrary and people are free to disagree on the details. It's a man-made idea, after all. But science lacks a few things that tend to constitute a religion. There is no underlying belief about the ultimate nature of the universe in science. There are no moral mandates. Science doesn't tell you how you should live your life, or what your purpose in life is. Science requires no worship. If we were to broaden our concept of religion to include "science" we would probably also have to include some other ideas under the heading of religion as well. 
